CONTEXT Permits INCLUDES Registry FROM "../contexts/registry_with_towns.adl" AS Reg,
                         Towns FROM "../contexts/towns.adl"
CONTEXT Permits IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Permits
{+ A chain of three contexts: Permits includes Registry, which includes Towns.
The data of Towns is part of what Permits sees.
To refer to a thing of Towns, Permits includes Towns itself.
That adds no database: it is the context that Registry includes. +}

RELATION applicant[Permit*Reg.Person] [UNI,TOT]
RELATION site[Permit*Towns.Town] [UNI]

POPULATION applicant[Permit*Reg.Person] CONTAINS [ ("permit1", "p1") ]
POPULATION site[Permit*Towns.Town] CONTAINS [ ("permit1", "Enschede") ]

RULE local : site |- applicant;Reg.residence
MEANING "A permit is for the town in which the applicant lives."
ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS local

RULE inProvince : site |- site;Towns.province;Towns.province~
MEANING "The town of a permit lies in a province."
ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS inProvince

ENDCONTEXT
